[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   TEP / Planet-9 -- step b14: environment checks
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   Two external-structure checks that the bias machinery has not
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   yet covered:
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   E1  The galactic tide.  The known external field acting on
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   outer solar-system orbits is the galactic tidal field --
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   quadrupolar, with preferred directions set by the galactic
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   plane, not a pointed direction.  If the detached cluster
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   were tidal, perihelia should organize relative to the
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   galactic equator/poles and the signature should be
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   axis-symmetric (m=2).  Test: galactic latitude of the
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   perihelion vectors vs isotropic and conditioned nulls;
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   plus the axis's own galactic position.
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   E2  The omega decomposition.  varpi = Om + w.  If the varpi
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   cluster were intrinsic and Om merely footprint-biased,
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   mean w should land near (mean varpi - mean Om) ~ 269 deg.
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   The observed mean w tells whether the w-clustering
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   (Trujillo-Sheppard element) is a trivial consequence or
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   carries independent structure.
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   Outputs: results/step_b14_environment_checks.json,
[2026-09-21 14:31:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 021]   figures/supplementary/step_b14_environment_checks.png
